{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-philippians-001",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 1,
  "title": "Philippians 1",
  "display_title": "Philippians 1",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "philippians",
  "book": "Philippians",
  "bookName": "Philippians",
  "bookOrder": 50,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 50001,
  "verseCount": 30,
  "aliases": [
    "Phil",
    "Php"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Paul and Timotheus, the servants of Jesus Christ, to all the saints in Christ Jesus which are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "I thank my God upon every remembrance of you,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Always in every prayer of mine for you all making request with joy,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For your fellowship in the gospel from the first day until now;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Even as it is meet for me to think this of you all, because I have you in my heart; inasmuch as both in my bonds, and in the defence and confirmation of the gospel, ye all are partakers of my grace.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For God is my record, how greatly I long after you all in the bowels of Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And this I pray, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and in all judgment;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "That ye may approve things that are excellent; that ye may be sincere and without offence till the day of Christ;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Being filled with the fruits of righteousness, which are by Jesus Christ, unto the glory and praise of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "But I would ye should understand, brethren, that the things which happened unto me have fallen out rather unto the furtherance of the gospel;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "So that my bonds in Christ are manifest in all the palace, and in all other places;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "And many of the brethren in the Lord, waxing confident by my bonds, are much more bold to speak the word without fear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Some indeed preach Christ even of envy and strife; and some also of good will:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The one preach Christ of contention, not sincerely, supposing to add affliction to my bonds:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "But the other of love, knowing that I am set for the defence of the gospel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "What then? notwithstanding, every way, whether in pretence, or in truth, Christ is preached; and I therein do rejoice, yea, and will rejoice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "For I know that this shall turn to my salvation through your prayer, and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "According to my earnest expectation and my hope, that in nothing I shall be ashamed, but that with all boldness, as always, so now also Christ shall be magnified in my body, whether it be by life, or by death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "But if I live in the flesh, this is the fruit of my labour: yet what I shall choose I wot not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For I am in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with Christ; which is far better:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Nevertheless to abide in the flesh is more needful for you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And having this confidence, I know that I shall abide and continue with you all for your furtherance and joy of faith;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "That your rejoicing may be more abundant in Jesus Christ for me by my coming to you again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Only let your conversation be as it becometh the gospel of Christ: that whether I come and see you, or else be absent, I may hear of your affairs, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "And in nothing terrified by your adversaries: which is to them an evident token of perdition, but to you of salvation, and that of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "For unto you it is given in the behalf of Christ, not only to believe on him, but also to suffer for his sake;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:philippians:1:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Having the same conflict which ye saw in me, and now hear to be in me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philippians 1:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philippians:1:30"
      }
    }
  ],
